hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16724","He said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from the daughter of Kardama, from her father, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I vowed to slaughter three of my camels; he said: If it was upon a gathering of the gatherings of the jahiliyya, or upon a festival of the festivals of the jahiliyya, or upon an idol, then no; and if it was upon other than that, then fulfill your vow; he said: O Messenger of Allah, upon the mother of this girl is walking, shall I walk on her behalf; he said: Yes."
